    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-sawyer-county-wi</guid>
    <pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>County board adopted an 18-month temporary moratorium on development of large data centers and associated infrastructure, to give staff time to draft setback, permitting and performance standards. Zoning committee had recommended it 5-0 on Jul 15. Source is meeting coverage, not the county&#x27;s own ordinance; end date is not stated in it</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Milwaukee: data center moratorium — Proposed</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/milwaukee-wi</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-milwaukee-wi</guid>
    <pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>Proposed ordinance would bar city departments from accepting or processing applications to construct, enlarge, expand, convert or occupy data centers, for one year after passage or until the zoning code is amended to regulate them, whichever comes first. Zoning Code Technical Committee endorsed it Aug 10; City Plan Commission hearing set for Sep 28, 2026. Common Council approval still required — not yet adopted</description>
  </item>
